From: Marek Czernohous <marek@czernohous.de>
Date: 2026-07-12
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/disp: soft-DPMS hold the flip event while blanked (NVAC/MCP79)

Patch 0015 suppresses background base-channel repaints while a soft_dpms head
is latched blanked, by forcing the plane back to its armed framebuffer in
nv50_disp_atomic_check (set.mask stays 0, so no base traffic and the fetch
engine is never parked).  That part works: 23 of 24 blank cycles over 128h of
uptime were clean, including a 20 hour blank.

But the commit tail still completed the per-crtc flip event for those
neutralised updates.  No flip ever reached the hardware, so this lies to
userspace: by DRM semantics a completed flip event means the previously scanned
framebuffer has been released.  The compositor therefore recycles that buffer
and renders into it -- while it is still the armed scanout framebuffer and thus
still pinned.  ttm_bo_validate() then rejects it:

	/* Moving of pinned BOs is forbidden */
	if (bo->pin_count)
		return -EINVAL;

which surfaces as:

	nouveau 0000:02:00.0: labwc[4376]: fail ttm_validate
	nouveau 0000:02:00.0: labwc[4376]: validating bo list
	nouveau 0000:02:00.0: labwc[4376]: validate: -22

Measured on a live system: 7 of 26 wakes hit this, and *every* validate reject
in the whole boot sat within 3s of a blank release -- none anywhere else.  The
user-visible effect is a stale, corrupted display after wake that a compositor
repaint cannot fix (the buffer is rejected); only restarting the client that
owns the poisoned buffer (e.g. swaybg) recovers it.

Fix the lie rather than the plane suppression: if the check neutralised the
update, hold the flip event back and deliver it from the wake bridge.  The
compositor then simply waits and stops repainting while blanked, which is the
desired behaviour anyway (it also stops it from burning power rendering frames
that are thrown away).  A new per-commit flag (asyh->soft_dpms_suppressed) marks
the neutralised commits so genuine commits, including the DPMS-off itself, are
untouched.

Holding the event means no further commit arrives, which would strand the
existing stale-latch failsafe in nv50_disp_atomic_check (it can only run on a
commit).  A delayed_work takes over that job, armed from the same
soft_dpms_blank_timeout_ms parameter (default 0 = off, behaviour unchanged).
When enabled it releases the latch and delivers the event, so a broken wake hook
cannot freeze the display forever; the trade-off is that suppression then ends
for the rest of that blank.

Holding a drm_pending_vblank_event across the blank is safe if the DRM file goes
away: drm_events_release() clears e->file_priv for events still on the pending
list, and drm_send_event_locked() then just frees it.

Depends on patches 0011 and 0015.  NVAC/MCP79 only, gated behind soft_dpms_blank.

Signed-off-by: Marek Czernohous <marek@czernohous.de>
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
---
diff -u -r a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/atom.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/atom.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/atom.h	2026-07-12 01:03:24.690704354 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/atom.h	2026-07-12 01:03:24.734771664 +0200
@@ -152,6 +152,12 @@
 	 * blank.  _off drives the DP sink to D3, _on retrains it to D0. */
 	bool soft_dpms_off:1;
 	bool soft_dpms_on:1;
+
+	/* soft-DPMS blank-suppression (patch 0017): set by nv50_disp_atomic_check
+	 * when it neutralised a plane update on this head because the head is
+	 * latched blanked.  The commit tail reads it to hold the flip event back:
+	 * no flip reached the hardware, so signalling one would lie to userspace. */
+	bool soft_dpms_suppressed:1;
 };
 
 static inline struct nv50_head_atom *
diff -u -r a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c	2026-07-12 01:03:24.660354070 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c	2026-07-12 01:03:24.744046384 +0200
@@ -2282,6 +2282,59 @@
 static struct nv50_head *nv50_soft_dpms_wake_head;
 static bool nv50_soft_dpms_any_asleep;
 
+/* Deliver a flip event that was held back while the head was latched blanked
+ * (patch 0017).  drm_crtc_send_vblank_event() must be called under
+ * dev->event_lock.  Safe even if the DRM file went away in the meantime:
+ * drm_events_release() clears e->file_priv, and drm_send_event_locked() then
+ * simply frees the event. */
+static void
+nv50_soft_dpms_send_held_event(struct nv50_head *head)
+{
+	struct drm_crtc *crtc = &head->base.base;
+	struct drm_pending_vblank_event *e;
+	unsigned long flags;
+
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&crtc->dev->event_lock, flags);
+	e = head->soft_dpms_event;
+	head->soft_dpms_event = NULL;
+	if (e)
+		drm_crtc_send_vblank_event(crtc, e);
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&crtc->dev->event_lock, flags);
+}
+
+/* Stale-latch failsafe (patch 0017).  Holding the flip event stops the
+ * compositor from committing, so the jiffies-based stale-latch check inside
+ * nv50_disp_atomic_check can never run again -- this timer takes over: release
+ * the latch and deliver the event so a missed wake hook cannot freeze the
+ * display forever.  Armed only when soft_dpms_blank_timeout_ms != 0 (default
+ * 0 = off, i.e. behaviour unchanged).  Trade-off when enabled: once it fires,
+ * suppression is over for the rest of the blank, so a background repaint can
+ * again park the base fetch engine.  Keep the timeout generous. */
+static void
+nv50_soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work_fn(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct nv50_head *head = container_of(to_delayed_work(work),
+					      struct nv50_head,
+					      soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work);
+
+	mutex_lock(&nv50_soft_dpms_wake_lock);
+	if (nv50_soft_dpms_wake_head == head)
+		nv50_soft_dpms_wake_head = NULL;
+	WRITE_ONCE(head->soft_dpms_asleep, false);
+	WRITE_ONCE(nv50_soft_dpms_any_asleep, false);
+	mutex_unlock(&nv50_soft_dpms_wake_lock);
+
+	nv50_soft_dpms_send_held_event(head);
+	pr_warn("nouveau: soft-dpms: wake missed, blank-suppression released by failsafe\n");
+}
+
+void
+nv50_soft_dpms_head_init(struct nv50_head *head)
+{
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&head->soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work,
+			  nv50_soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work_fn);
+}
+
 static int
 nv50_soft_dpms_wake_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 {
@@ -2298,6 +2351,14 @@
 	WRITE_ONCE(nv50_soft_dpms_any_asleep, false);
 	mutex_unlock(&nv50_soft_dpms_wake_lock);
 
+	/* patch 0017: the wake arrived -- cancel the failsafe and hand the
+	 * compositor the flip event we held back while blanked, so it resumes
+	 * repainting with a correct view of which buffers it owns. */
+	if (head) {
+		cancel_delayed_work(&head->soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work);
+		nv50_soft_dpms_send_held_event(head);
+	}
+
 	pr_info("nouveau: soft-dpms: blank-suppression released (wake bridge)\n");
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -2560,6 +2621,52 @@
 	}
 
 	for_each_new_crtc_in_state(state, crtc, new_crtc_state, i) {
+		struct nv50_head *nvh = nv50_head(crtc);
+
+		/* soft-DPMS blank-suppression flip-event hold (patch 0017): the check
+		 * neutralised this update because the head is latched blanked, so no
+		 * flip reached the hardware.  Completing the event would tell the
+		 * compositor its previous buffer is free; it would recycle that buffer
+		 * and render into the framebuffer that is STILL pinned for scanout ->
+		 * ttm_bo_validate() -> -EINVAL.  Hold the event instead: the compositor
+		 * waits and stops repainting while blanked (which is what we want), and
+		 * the wake bridge delivers it.  Drop the vblank reference taken earlier
+		 * -- we are not waiting on a flip we never programmed. */
+		if (nouveau_soft_dpms && nouveau_soft_dpms_blank &&
+		    new_crtc_state->event &&
+		    nv50_head_atom(new_crtc_state)->soft_dpms_suppressed &&
+		    READ_ONCE(nvh->soft_dpms_asleep)) {
+			unsigned int tmo = READ_ONCE(nouveau_soft_dpms_blank_timeout_ms);
+			unsigned long flags;
+			bool held = false;
+
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&crtc->dev->event_lock, flags);
+			if (!nvh->soft_dpms_event) {
+				nvh->soft_dpms_event = new_crtc_state->event;
+				held = true;
+			}
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&crtc->dev->event_lock, flags);
+
+			if (held) {
+				new_crtc_state->event = NULL;
+				if (new_crtc_state->active)
+					drm_crtc_vblank_put(crtc);
+				if (tmo)
+					mod_delayed_work(system_wq,
+							 &nvh->soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work,
+							 msecs_to_jiffies(tmo));
+				continue;
+			}
+			/* One is already held (a compositor that did not wait for it):
+			 * fall through and complete this one normally rather than leak. */
+		}
+
+		/* Suppression ended (wake, modeset exemption or failsafe) while an
+		 * event was still held: deliver it now so nobody waits forever. */
+		if (READ_ONCE(nvh->soft_dpms_event) &&
+		    !READ_ONCE(nvh->soft_dpms_asleep))
+			nv50_soft_dpms_send_held_event(nvh);
+
 		if (new_crtc_state->event) {
 			unsigned long flags;
 			/* Get correct count/ts if racing with vblank irq */
@@ -2893,6 +3000,12 @@
 			new_plane_state->src_y  = armed->src_y;
 			new_plane_state->src_w  = armed->src_w;
 			new_plane_state->src_h  = armed->src_h;
+
+			/* patch 0017: tell the commit tail that this update was
+			 * neutralised, so it holds the flip event back instead of
+			 * signalling a flip that never happened. */
+			if (pcs)
+				nv50_head_atom(pcs)->soft_dpms_suppressed = true;
 		}
 	}
 
diff -u -r a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.c	2026-07-12 01:03:24.679764924 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.c	2026-07-12 01:03:24.736133783 +0200
@@ -494,6 +494,9 @@
 	 * reads them indeterminate. */
 	asyh->soft_dpms_off = false;
 	asyh->soft_dpms_on  = false;
+	/* patch 0017: per-commit too -- a stale bit here would hold a flip event
+	 * back on a commit that was never suppressed. */
+	asyh->soft_dpms_suppressed = false;
 	return &asyh->state;
 }
 
@@ -590,6 +593,7 @@
 	head->func = disp->core->func->head;
 	head->disp = disp;
 	head->base.index = index;
+	nv50_soft_dpms_head_init(head);
 
 	if (disp->disp->object.oclass < GF110_DISP)
 		funcs = &nv50_head_func;
diff -u -r a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.h	2026-07-12 01:03:24.684680296 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/head.h	2026-07-12 01:03:24.735221531 +0200
@@ -30,8 +30,26 @@
 	 * stamps the latch time so a missed wake cannot suppress forever. */
 	bool soft_dpms_asleep;
 	unsigned long soft_dpms_blank_jiffies;
+
+	/* soft-DPMS blank-suppression flip-event hold (patch 0017).  While the head
+	 * is latched blanked the check neutralises plane updates, so no flip reaches
+	 * the hardware.  Completing the flip event anyway makes the compositor
+	 * believe its previous buffer was released; it recycles that buffer and
+	 * renders into the framebuffer that is STILL pinned for scanout, which
+	 * ttm_bo_validate() rejects with -EINVAL ("Moving of pinned BOs is
+	 * forbidden").  Hold the event here instead and deliver it on wake.
+	 * Serialised by dev->event_lock.
+	 *
+	 * blank_timeout_work is the matching failsafe: with an event held the
+	 * compositor stops committing, so the stale-latch check inside
+	 * nv50_disp_atomic_check can never run again.  The timer takes over that
+	 * job.  Armed only when soft_dpms_blank_timeout_ms != 0 (default 0 = off). */
+	struct drm_pending_vblank_event *soft_dpms_event;
+	struct delayed_work soft_dpms_blank_timeout_work;
 };
 
+void nv50_soft_dpms_head_init(struct nv50_head *head);
+
 struct nv50_head *nv50_head_create(struct drm_device *, int index);
 void nv50_head_flush_set(struct nv50_head *head, struct nv50_head_atom *asyh);
 void nv50_head_flush_set_wndw(struct nv50_head *head, struct nv50_head_atom *asyh);
